{
  "info": {
    "name": "Yeet Casino bet processor",
    "description": "Manual harness for the Yeet take-home. Every PDF acceptance scenario, both report endpoints, and the health checks.\n\n**How HMAC signing works in this collection:** a single pre-request script at the collection level signs every POST/GET body with HMAC_SHA256(secret, raw body). The `secret` and `baseUrl` are collection variables — set them in the collection's *Variables* tab if you want anything other than the defaults (`test` and `http://localhost:3000`).\n\n**Skipping HMAC on demand:** the missing/invalid-auth scenarios set a request-level `skipHmac` variable so the pre-request leaves the Authorization header alone. Health endpoints are detected by URL and never signed (the server skips HMAC for them).\n\n**Report date range:** the report folder's pre-request script populates `reportFrom` / `reportTo` to cover the current UTC day, so requests work immediately without manual date entry.\n\nStart the API first (`docker compose up --build` or `node dist/main.js`), seed at least the acceptance user (`npm run seed -- --users 1`), then run requests top to bottom.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Health endpoints are @SkipHmac'd server-side.",
          "const url = pm.request.url.toString();",
          "if (/\\/(health|ready)(\\?|$)/.test(url)) {",
          "    return;",
          "}",
          "",
          "// Per-request opt-outs are encoded as static request headers so",
          "// nothing leaks between requests in the same iteration:",
          "//   X-Skip-Hmac: true             — leave Authorization untouched (or absent)",
          "//   X-Override-Hmac: <full value> — replace Authorization with this value verbatim",
          "// Postman's pre-request scripts run collection → folder → request,",
          "// which makes request-level variable opt-outs leaky; headers are",
          "// part of the request definition and visible here immediately.",
          "const skipHeader = pm.request.headers.get('X-Skip-Hmac');",
          "if (skipHeader === 'true') {",
          "    pm.request.headers.remove('X-Skip-Hmac');",
          "    pm.request.headers.remove('Authorization');",
          "    return;",
          "}",
          "const overrideHeader = pm.request.headers.get('X-Override-Hmac');",
          "if (overrideHeader) {",
          "    pm.request.headers.remove('X-Override-Hmac');",
          "    pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Authorization', value: overrideHeader });",
          "    return;",
          "}",
          "",
          "const secret = pm.collectionVariables.get('secret') || 'test';",
          "",
          "// Resolve any {{vars}} in the raw body the same way Postman would",
          "// when it actually sends the request, so the HMAC matches the bytes",
          "// on the wire.",
          "let body = '';",
          "if (pm.request.body && pm.request.body.mode === 'raw' && pm.request.body.raw) {",
          "    body = pm.request.body.raw.replace(/\\{\\{([^}]+)\\}\\}/g, function (_, name) {",
          "        const v = pm.variables.get(name.trim());",
          "        return v === undefined ? '' : v;",
          "    });",
          "}",
          "",
          "const hex = CryptoJS.HmacSHA256(body, secret).toString(CryptoJS.enc.Hex);",
          "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Authorization', value: 'HMAC-SHA256 ' + hex });"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "secret", "value": "test", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "8|USDT|USD", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health  (liveness)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["health"] }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /ready  (readiness — pings the DB)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/ready", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["ready"] }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
